From: nabu port
Subject: [PATCH 0012] nabu: physmap slack for twig-aligned regions with ARM_LARGE_MEMORY

macOS targets build with ARM_LARGE_MEMORY. Without a PPL monitor, the
"virtual machine" layout sets physmap_end = physmap_base + real_phys_size,
while arm_vm_physmap_slide() shifts every region so its VA keeps its PA
offset within a 32 MiB twig (16 KiB pages). Under QEMU (cortex-a76, 1 GiB
DarwinBoot window) the NABU kernel stopped in arm_vm_physmap_init:
"arm_vm_init.c:1642 Assertion failed: (temp_ptov_table[ptov_index - 1].va
+ ...len) <= physmap_end" with physmap_base 0xfffffdf01d25c000, physmap_end
0xfffffdf05d25c000, segLOWEST == gVirtBase. The overflow depends on the
random physmap slide. NABU now reserves PTOV_TABLE_SIZE twigs of slack, as
the !ARM_LARGE_MEMORY layout does; the reserved L1 range (64 GiB) has room.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c b/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
index 756af52..f0c260f 100644
--- a/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
@@ -1885,6 +1885,15 @@ arm_vm_init(uint64_t memory_size, boot_args * args)
 	/* For large memory systems with no PPL such as virtual machines */
 	static_memory_end = phystokv(args->topOfKernelData);
 	physmap_end = physmap_base + real_phys_size;
+#if defined(NABU)
+	/*
+	 * arm_vm_physmap_slide() moves each region so its VA keeps its PA offset
+	 * within a twig (32 MiB with 16 KiB pages). Without the slack that the
+	 * !ARM_LARGE_MEMORY layout reserves, the last region can end past
+	 * physmap_end depending on the random physmap slide.
+	 */
+	physmap_end += (PTOV_TABLE_SIZE * ARM_TT_TWIG_SIZE);
+#endif /* NABU */
 #else
 	static_memory_end = physmap_base + mem_size + (PTOV_TABLE_SIZE * ARM_TT_TWIG_SIZE); // worst possible case for block alignment
 	physmap_end = physmap_base + real_phys_size + (PTOV_TABLE_SIZE * ARM_TT_TWIG_SIZE);
